{
  "case_id": "2021-21-309",
  "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Southwest Airlines",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1 of the FAA exempts only classes of workers that work on an instrumentality of foreign or interstate commerce, like a plane, ship, or train, as it moves goods or people across borders."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Southwest Airlines",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We know that because \"seamen\" was a term of art. It meant workers who predominantly worked on a vessel. Vessels, by definition, transported or were capable of transporting goods or people over water. And the paradigmatic seamen, as the Court noted in Chandris, sailed long voyages."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now what evidence is there that railroad workers who did that were or were not covered by this statutory language? And, if they were covered by it, do you lose?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What about ticket agents? Are they included as transport workers under your approach?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: In your answers to the Chief Justice, you have two arguments, alternative arguments. Are you distinguishing your broader \"all airline workers\" from your narrower argument, or am I misreading how you constructed your -- your argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: But, on your narrower argument, just to follow up on the Chief Justice's questions, on your narrower argument, does that bring in then the gate ticket agents, or is that a question for another day, or where does that stand?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Southwest",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And what Southwest argues is that, well, those cases aren't under this particular statute. But, of course, they're not. This particular statute didn't exist. But this -- but Congress, knowing how this Court had interpreted the phrase \"engaged in interstate commerce,\" \"engaged in foreign commerce,\" nevertheless used those words."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What -- to what industries would it apply besides the airlines?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: How -- how do you distinguish -- trucking is in -- you say trucking is in the exemption."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If everybody who worked for the Cunard line was covered, what would be the point of -- or that's not a -- that's a passenger shipping line."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Suppose it said seamen, railroad engineers, and others engaged in interstate or foreign commerce. Would everybody who worked for the railroad be covered?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So would -- would -- assume two things for me."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: I have a historical question you --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Shay Dvoretzky",
      "case_id": "2021-21-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ddef3554d3b-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DVORETZKY: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. A few points in rebuttal."
    },
